# Formerly pinned 0 1 0, calls 1 (slice 413): take(p) ran by W; the opened reading was hidden by the rule
# R89, opening is an attempt -- the one field of the Structure p refers to would take the formal value the
# whole took. TZ 2026-11-19 §9.3 withdraws it: p is a reference to a Structure (Model), not supplied by
# assignment, so E is weighed; its fields are the actuals (none by the norm; the kernel exposes one) and
# value is optional with no default: admitted (§9.4); W is admitted too: two candidates of one declaration,
# ambiguity 3 (§9.5; §9.8, the row «W и E подходят одному объявлению»); nothing runs, calls 0. The whole
# goes by assignment, take(value := p) (select_named_whole). Derived from the norm at the build of step
# 21.5, after its first row run (opus; accepted by fable 2026-11-22).
int: calls 0
@: Model ()
fn: take (@: value Model) int
    node\calls := node\calls + 1
    return: 9
sub: main () (const: (@: p Model); int: r 0)
    r := take(p)
main()
